\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\f0\fs24\cf0
\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Fanny Heaslip Lea}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 She made a little shadow-hidden grave,}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 The day Faith died;}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Therein she laid it, heard the clod\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s sick fall,}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 And smiled aside-}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93If less I ask,\u8221\'94}{\f1\fs24\b1\i0\cf1  tear-blind, }{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 she mocked, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I may be less denied.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 She set a rose to blossom in her hair,}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 The day Faith died-}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Now glad,\u8221\'94 she said, \u8220\'93And free at last, I go,}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 And life is wide.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 But through long nights she stared into the dark,}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 And she knew she lied.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 She sat very straight in a winged chair richly covered with petit point, her elicate claw-like hands lay lightly folded on her silken lap, and her eyes\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8230\'85 the eyes of an old lady eagle who has looked long and perhaps not too discreetly on the sun.. Showed a slight grayish glaze. Which meat that the read had lasted nearly its appointed two hours and the attention of the Marchesa was teetering.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93He\u8217\'92s strong meat,\u8221\'94 said the Marchesa, wagging gray curls above a  withered throat, perennially swathed in a black velvet band\u8230\'85 \u8220\'93Strong meat, Swinburne, \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0  too strong for your type, Miss wayne. Just as well let him be. Read-ah, WOrdsworth\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 if you must!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Miss wayne continued doggedly, with a lift of the dark eyebrows which dismised Wordsworth in silence: \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93\u8217\'92\u8230\'85What saved Carlyle, Macaulay and company is as plain as day. They were first-rate artists. THey could make the thing charming, and that is awlays a million times more important than making it true.\u8217\'92\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93There!\u8221\'94 cried the Marchesa and lifted a dramtic little old forefinger by way of ringing down the curtain on the afternoon\u8217\'92s performance. \u8220\'93Let us stop on that! That\u8217\'92s a very subtle statement, indeed. I like it. This Mencken did you say his name was?\u8221\'94\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Younf, pulchritudinous and irresistible.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Romance lived in that room and lurked like a splinter of tarnished starlight in the Marchesa\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s knowledgable glance.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8220\'93 insisted the Marchesa, between avid, bird-like sips and fierce small crunchings\u8230\'85 \u8220\'93should any woman wish to be seventy?\u8230\'85}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 The Marchesa looked vaguely about her\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8230\'85 at the darkly gleaming piano in the farhter corner, with a faded Spnish shawl thrown across it\u8230\'85 at the tea-table, loaded with heavy repousse silver and fragile Dresden cups\u8230\'85 at the French prints, ornately framed, adorning the walls\u8230\'85 at the heart-shaped and circular cushions of Normandy lace crowding the brocaded chaise longue\u8230\'85.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1}